Package: VIBER
Type: Package
Title: VIBER: Variational Inference for Binomial Mixtures
Version: 1.0.1
Date: 2026-07-01
Maintainer: Giulio Caravagna <gcaravagn@gmail.com>
Authors@R: c(
    person("Giulio", "Caravagna", email = "gcaravagn@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Nicola", "Calonaci", email = "nicola.calonaci@gmail.com", role = "ctb"),
    person("Elena", "Buscaroli", email = "ele.buscaroli@gmail.com", role = "ctb"))
Description: Implements the variational Bayesian framework described in
    Caravagna et al. (2020) <doi:10.1038/s41588-020-0675-5> to fit
    multi-variate Binomial mixture models. The statistical model is
    semi-parametric and fitted by a variational mean-field approximation to
    the model posterior. Mixture components are Binomial distributions that
    can model multi-dimensional count data, for instance sequencing read
    counts in cancer genomics. The package provides functions to fit and
    visualise clustering results.
